msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:86
msgid ""
"Accepts ``None`` (a surface representation), a name from :data:"
"`REPRESENTATION_TYPES`, or a representation class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:93
msgid ""
"*color* is either a 3-sequence with components in ``[0, 1]`` or a snake_case "
"named color from :mod:`vtkmodules.util.colors` (e.g. ``\"tomato\"``, "
"``\"steel_blue\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:100
msgid ""
"Attribute assignment on a Python subclass of a VTK object quietly creates an "
"instance attribute, which would turn a misspelled keyword argument into a "
"property that silently does nothing.  Keyword arguments are checked here so "
"that they fail where the mistake was made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:108
msgid ""
"The C++ classes carry only what it takes to make data visible and legible; "
"everything else lives on the actor, property, mapper or filter underneath. "
"That is the right shape for C++, where reaching one object further is a "
"method call, but it would spoil ``view.show(src, specular=0.3)`` in Python, "
"where flat keyword arguments are the whole point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:114
msgid ""
"So an attribute this class does not define is looked for on each delegate in "
"turn, and set on the first that has it.  ``rep.specular = 0.3`` and ``rep."
"property.specular = 0.3`` are then the same thing, and an attribute nobody "
"owns still fails, naming the delegates it looked in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:108
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:155
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:197
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:271
msgid "Initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:112
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:159
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:201
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:275
msgid "Accept in the constructor everything assignment accepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:114
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:161
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:203
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:277
msgid ""
"VTK builds its own constructor keyword handling from the properties a class "
"declares, and it runs before any Python attribute assignment -- so it never "
"reaches the delegation below, and ``view.specular = 0.3`` would work while "
"``Class(specular=0.3)`` did not.  Anything VTK does not recognise is applied "
"here instead, which puts the two back in step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:120
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:167
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:209
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:283
msgid ""
"A dict value configures the sub-object of that name, so the grouping the C++ "
"API has is available at construction too::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:123
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:170
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:212
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:286
msgid ""
"view = vtkScivisView(\n"
"    window_title=\"demo\",\n"
"    selector={\"mode\": \"frustum\"},\n"
"    light_kit={\"key_light_intensity\": 0.8},\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:129
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:176
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:218
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:292
msgid ""
"There is no way to spell that as a keyword name -- ``selector.mode=`` is a "
"syntax error -- and a dict means nothing to an ordinary VTK property, so "
"there is nothing for it to collide with."
msgstr ""

